{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions","id":1033798,"title":"Can Ghouls Learn Devotions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-17T18:51:16-08:00","id":1033798,"title":"Can Ghouls Learn Devotions?","content":"Exactly what it says in the title - can Ghouls be taught how to use Devotions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T22:05:35-08:00","id":1033882,"title":"","content":"I don't believe so, I'd have to check the book to be certain though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T22:11:13-08:00","id":1033883,"title":"","content":"The book doesn't say they can't. It doesn't really say that they can either though. I'd probably allow it if a player asked, but I'd probably say they need a teacher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T23:41:06-08:00","id":1033899,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Half Damned will answer that question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:03:03-08:00","id":1034196,"title":"","content":"I see no reason for not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:51:47-08:00","id":1034298,"title":"","content":"Assuming that they meet the Discipline prereqs, I do not see why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 01-18-2017, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:44:38-08:00","id":1034708,"title":"","content":"I would say that they can, because there is a small list of what they can't learn and if devotions weren't allowed I feel like that would have been included on that list.<br /> <br /> Devotions are ultimately part of the discipline family and ghouls can learn disciplines the way vampires do. (with blood or a teacher... or both )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 01-19-2017, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:54:57-08:00","id":1034716,"title":"","content":"I'd rule they can with a vampire teacher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T07:24:54-08:00","id":1035212,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, revenants can't learn devotions and there's no &quot;unless they knew them as a ghoul&quot; clause. <br /> <br /> Doesn't feel right for ghouls to be able to do it when revenants can't, IMHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T07:43:39-08:00","id":1035218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035212#post1035212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, revenants can't learn devotions and there's no &quot;unless they knew them as a ghoul&quot; clause.<br /> <br /> Doesn't feel right for ghouls to be able to do it when revenants can't, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Keep in mind that while ghouls have serious problems, revenants are seriously cursed--they're not just some kind of half-vampire but are more like 90% hungry beast and a rapidly fading sense of man in there somewhere. Ghouls are 90% man with something weird and feral scrabbling to get out.<br /> <br /> That said, ghouls have in the past been forbidden to use disciplines that require spilling vitae, because their blood is not vitae. I could see that easily preventing certain devotions. Others, well, are just extensions or adaptations of existing Disciplines, so could be taught. You'd only want to imagine a ghoul inventing a new devotion under very unusual circumstances (centuries-old, long-term exposure to high-potency vitae, other supernatural influences, etc.). <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf <br /> <br /> PS. Of course, it's your story and this is really a small point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:10:30-08:00","id":1035226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035212#post1035212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, revenants can't learn devotions and there's no &quot;unless they knew them as a ghoul&quot; clause.<br /> <br /> Doesn't feel right for ghouls to be able to do it when revenants can't, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls are not Revenants. I wouldn't base judgement on what one or the other can do because of the other. They aren't the same thing at all. They are created differently, they have a completely different rule base. One is alive, one is dead. I am sure that we will get more information on this in the half-damned book, but for now. I would say that since ghouls learn disciplines as vampires do, except that they can not USE the ones that spill vitae, they can still learn devotions as a vampire would.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Ghouls can use most Disciplines, including bloodline<br /> Disciplines, but suffer some restrictions.<br /> <br /> <b>Learning Disciplines: </b>Ghouls may learn Disciplines under<br /> the same rules as Kindred. <u>They may not learn Coils or Scales<br /> of the Dragon.</u><br /> <br /> <br /> Spilling Blood: If a Discipline power requires the user to<br /> spill blood or feed it to someone (such as Raise the Familiar),<br /> the ghoul may not use it. You as a player may buy the power on<br /> the way to purchasing another one, however.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Many vampires develop the abilities listed here for each<br /> Discipline, but some manifest new powers of the Blood. These<br /> new Discipline techniques, called Devotions, can manifest<br /> spontaneously in some Kindred, or can be developed by<br /> careful honing of Discipline abilities.<u><b> Once a vampire knows<br /> a Devotion, she can teach it to another Kindred in much the<br /> same way as the standard Discipline techniques</b></u></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 01-20-2017, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:15:06-08:00","id":1035265,"title":"","content":"Now, see, I can read all that and come to the exact opposite conclusion.<br /> <br /> Ghouls learn <i>disciplines</i> under the same rules as kindred.<br /> <br /> Vampires can teach devotions <i>to other kindred</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines</b><b> are not devotions</b>. They are learned the same way <i>for vampires</i>, but nothing says they can be taught to ghouls at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 01-20-2017, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:47:55-08:00","id":1035280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035265#post1035265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, see, I can read all that and come to the exact opposite conclusion.<br /> <br /> Ghouls learn <i>disciplines</i> under the same rules as kindred.<br /> <br /> Vampires can teach devotions <i>to other kindred</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines</b><b> are not devotions</b>. They are learned the same way <i>for vampires</i>, but nothing says they can be taught to ghouls at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't want to be a pain, but if something says &quot;follow the same rules as kindred&quot; then when it says , &quot;can teach to other kindred&quot; you are following those rules, and thus ghouls apply there. Because it specifically says to follow those rules. <br /> <br /> By your logic when it says the following as it consistently uses the word Kindred, that ghouls can't learn them at all because no where does it say ghouls. But since it told us to use the same rules as the kindred would use, we can use these same rules as if the ghoul was kindred. because again.. it specifically said to do that. <br /> <br /> <i>Many <b>Kindred </b>spontaneously manifest new Disciplines, as<br /> the Beast asserts itself in new and strange ways. The Blood<br /> makes strong connections between <b>vampires</b>, so most <b>Kindred</b><br /> only display the Disciplines of their Clan. To learn another<br /> Discipline, the vampire must first track down another vampire<br /> who possesses the Discipline and drink at least one point of his<br /> Vitae \u2014 with all of the attendant consequences. </i><br /> <br /> Devotions are &quot;Discipline techniques&quot; They are new ways to use the discipline. An example would be Money. A devotion would be dollar bills. I have to have money in order to get dollar bills, just dollars are specialized money, but still money. Hmm maybe a better example of a devotion would be a 2 dollar bill or a silver dollar as they are more rare... <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T10:03:15-08:00","id":1035290,"title":"","content":"From the perspective of a vampire, disciplines = devotions.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of a discipline, ghouls = vampires.<br /> <br /> But from the perspective of a ghoul disciplines =/= devotions, and from the perspective of a devotion ghouls =/= vampires.<br /> <br /> Ghouls are treated as vampires by disciplines <i>but</i> <i>not devotions, </i>and devotions are treated as disciplines by vampires <i>but not ghouls.</i><br /> <br /> To use your money analogy, a Scottish pound counts as a pound in Scotland but not England, whereas an English pound works in both.<br /> <br /> Scotland is a vampire, English pounds are disciplines, Scottish pounds are devotions, England is a ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 01-20-2017, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T10:32:44-08:00","id":1035304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035290#post1035290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the perspective of a vampire, disciplines = devotions.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of a discipline, ghouls = vampires.<br /> <br /> But from the perspective of a ghoul disciplines =/= devotions, and from the perspective of a devotion ghouls =/= vampires.<br /> <br /> Ghouls are treated as vampires by disciplines <i>but</i> <i>not devotions, </i>and devotions are treated as disciplines by vampires <i>but not ghouls.</i><br /> <br /> To use your money analogy, a Scottish pound counts as a pound in Scotland but not England, whereas an English pound works in both.<br /> <br /> Scotland is a vampire, English pounds are disciplines, Scottish pounds are devotions, England is a ghoul.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps we are going to get a little confusing here, but no? Because Majesty for a ghoul and Majesty for a vampire are... exactly the same. They do not change from ghoul to vampire to even a revenant. They are all just Majesty. So when Saying Scotland uses A money and England uses B money because they are different countries... it implies they are too using different disciplines when they are not. They are using the exact same discipline.<br /> <br /> You might have been better off with saying New York and New Mexico because they are not the same state, but they still use the same money. As Money is the discipline and it is exactly the same across the board for everyone who uses it.<br /> The people in New York and the people in New Mexico can both earn the exact same kind of money, even though they are different and have their own rules/laws, but the money will always be the same.<br /> <br /> Perhaps we should ditch the analogy and say Majesty is the discipline, Idol is a standard Discipline technique and Summoning is a Discipline technique. even though it is a devotion and not everyone has it, but not everyone has Idol either...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 01-20-2017, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T10:46:59-08:00","id":1035309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035280#post1035280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Devotions are &quot;Discipline techniques&quot; They are new ways to use the discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Most of the time they are combinations of two or more disciplines to create an effect that otherwise couldn't be accomplished just by turning on the relevant powers all at once. Or they entail the use of coils or sorcery rituals, which are something ghouls cannot use at all or are restricted. The only argument you could make that it's a &quot;new&quot; way to use a discipline in if you're referring to single discipline devotions that splinter or produce more effects the higher up you go in the pre-requisites. <br /> <br /> I personally don't care one way or the other about ghouls learning devotions but I don't see anything in the rules permitting it. Devotions don't say Kindred only nor but there is no mention of them being able to learn them while it is expressly said they can learn disciplines if they're taught. That leads me to the conclusion that it's up for STs to decide as opposed to ghoul players simply being able to demand access to them out of a sense of rules backed entitlement. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T10:51:33-08:00","id":1035311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035309#post1035309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. Most of the time they are combinations of two or more disciplines to create an effect that otherwise couldn't be accomplished just by turning on the relevant powers all at once. Or they entail the use of coils or sorcery rituals, which are something ghouls cannot use at all or are restricted. The only argument you could make that it's a &quot;new&quot; way to use a discipline in if you're referring to single discipline devotions that splinter or produce more effects the higher up you go in the pre-requisites.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The book literally tells us they are &quot;Discipline Techniques&quot; None of them use the coils or rituals.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;These new <u>Discipline techniques</u>, called Devotions, can manifest<br /> spontaneously in some Kindred, or can be developed by<br /> careful honing of Discipline abilities.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also the book literally says, <i>&quot; Once a vampire knows<br /> a Devotion, she can teach it to another Kindred in much the<br /> same way as the <u>standard Discipline techniques</u>. &quot;</i><br /> <br /> Meaning the &quot;normal&quot; uses of the disciplines are the &quot;standard Discipline techniques&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035309#post1035309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally don't care one way or the other about ghouls learning devotions but I don't see anything in the rules permitting it. Devotions don't say Kindred only nor but there is no mention of them being able to learn them while it is expressly said they can learn disciplines if they're taught. That leads me to the conclusion that it's up for STs to decide as opposed to ghoul players simply being able to demand access to them out of a sense of rules backed entitlement.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do not understand how people can say it's not in the book when it says directly, ghouls learn exactly the same way a vampire does except they can not learn scales and coils.( not except, coils, scales and devotions )<br /> <br /> It even goes as far as to tell us that they can even learn disciplines like blood sorcery even if they can't use it. If it was meant to be like a revenant why would they not say &quot;They can learn disciplines they way a revenant can&quot; One word would not have changed the book at all, but ghouls entirely. They are meant to be like the kindred and specifically have a list of what they can not do.. Why would devotions not be on that list?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 01-20-2017, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:59:09-08:00","id":1035353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035304#post1035304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Perhaps we are going to get a little confusing here, but no? Because Majesty for a ghoul and Majesty for a vampire are... exactly the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>And an English pound in Scotland is exactly the same as an English pound in England. Likewise a Scottish pound in Scotland is exactly the same as an English pound in Scotland.<br /> <br /> <i>But </i>a Scottish pound in England is n<i>ot</i> the same as an English pound in England. <br /> <br /> An English pound treats scotland an England the same, Just like a discipline treats a vampire and a ghoul the same.<br /> <br /> A Scottish pound is a specific sort of pound, like a devotion is a specific discipline power. Scottish pounds <i>only work in Scotland</i> just like devotions can be taught as if they were disciplines To Vampires.<br /> <br /> A=B if X<br /> <br /> and X=Y if A <br /> <br /> <i><b>does not mean</b> </i><br /> <br /> that A=B if Y. <br /> <br /> Devotions can be taught as if they were disciplines <b>TO VAMPIRES. </b><i>Only Vampires. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:08:02-08:00","id":1035358,"title":"","content":"I don't use the word KINDRED interchangeably to refer to all the other blood slurping monsters like thralls, strix, ghouls, hopping corpses, revenants, and so on that are mentioned. If the term was meant to be interchangeable, it would be used to describe them respectively. It's not, more often than not it's used to highlight the differences between them.<br /> There is ZERO MENTION of ghouls learning devotions. Your quotes only mentions teaching other Kindred. <br /> If ghouls are like kindred in every way except for a meaningless and superficial mechanic, then they would be a distinct clan and would be designated as such. Not given a separate entry in the back of the book with a list of caveats and addendums occasionally littered throughout the book exempting them from certain mechanical situations that apply to &quot;mortals&quot; or other kindred.<br /> <br /> And btw, disciplines DON'T work the same for ghouls. By your own admission, they can't use certain powers because they're incapable of performing the attendant action. They also function at diminished capacity or fail outright if their target is another kindred. And resist the applications of those powers by others is reduced because they lack the Power Stat.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Devotion\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Devotion</a><br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":".  Added link 01-20-2017, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:27:03-08:00","id":1035378,"title":"","content":"I work in a shop in England and we take Scotish pounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:26:27-08:00","id":1035413,"title":"","content":"How far north are you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T15:18:24-08:00","id":1035481,"title":"","content":"Worcestershire in the midlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T15:35:10-08:00","id":1035487,"title":"","content":"The only Vampires I know for certain that can't learn to use devotions, are Cruac Gods, although it doesn't appear Void Creatures can either, but it specifically says Cruac Gods can't learn devotions. <br /> <br /> Ghouls, Dhampyrs, and Reverants will likely be answered in half damned. <br /> <br /> Strix are a maybe. <br /> <br /> The Jiang Shi are Kindred like enough to do so I believe. They might be in the process of becoming a new clan of Kindred after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T15:40:20-08:00","id":1035489,"title":"","content":"Strix definitely can. They get 3 experiences worth for every discipline slot they spend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T15:56:06-08:00","id":1035495,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah that's right. So Kindred, Jiang Shi, and Strix are a yes, Cruac Gods are a no, Void Creatures are a likely no, same with that Belial Theban Sorcery Familiars, Ghouls/Reverants/Dympyrs will hopefully be answered in half damned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T16:07:56-08:00","id":1035500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035358#post1035358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't use the word KINDRED interchangeably to refer to all the other blood slurping monsters like thralls, strix, ghouls, hopping corpses, revenants, and so on that are mentioned. If the term was meant to be interchangeable, it would be used to describe them respectively. It's not, more often than not it's used to highlight the differences between them.<br /> There is ZERO MENTION of ghouls learning devotions. Your quotes only mentions teaching other Kindred.<br /> If ghouls are like kindred in every way except for a meaningless and superficial mechanic, then they would be a distinct clan and would be designated as such. Not given a separate entry in the back of the book with a list of caveats and addendums occasionally littered throughout the book exempting them from certain mechanical situations that apply to &quot;mortals&quot; or other kindred.<br /> <br /> And btw, disciplines DON'T work the same for ghouls. By your own admission, they can't use certain powers because they're incapable of performing the attendant action. They also function at diminished capacity or fail outright if their target is another kindred. And resist the applications of those powers by others is reduced because they lack the Power Stat.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Devotion\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Devotion</a><br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am not sure what that wiki is, but I generally don't look at Wiki's online because half the time I can't tell if they are Old Wod or New wod or Chronicles. So I tend to look directly in the book... which everyone seems to be ignoring the fact that the book states:<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Learning Disciplines: Ghouls may learn Disciplines under the same rules as Kindred. </b></i>They may not learn Coils or Scales of the Dragon. Page 297<br /> <br /> <br /> So that means everything in the section where it describes how Kindred learn disciplines is EXACTLY THE SAME for a ghoul. How is this not recognized? I did not say that kindred was an interchangeable word to be tossed around whenever all willynilly. I did not say that ghouls are kindred... I said the book said to follow the same rules as the kindred<br /> <br /> The book specifically says to refer to that section of the book and use it. Basic reading comprehension means that if it says to use those rules for how a ghoul worKs, then when it says vampires can teach to other vampires. It means vampires can teach to ghouls too...<br /> <br /> I don't get how we are all ignoring that line? And if i am not reading it correctly: What does it mean?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Do let me know how Majesty is different for a vampire and a ghoul? What are the different mechanical functions? Where can I find how the rest of the disciplines work for Ghouls. Besides failing against a vampire they are mechanically 100% the same. Charm still charms. Dominate still Dominates. Protean still.... proteans? I think you misunderstood me<br /> <br /> But this is a perfect teachable example because you said they work the same EXCEPT in these certain situations. So when it says ghouls learn the way vampires do EXCEPT when it's Ordo stuff... that would mean all instances where it says a vampire can teach a vampire would mean a vampire can teach a ghoul.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, If am wrong tell me what this <i><b> Ghouls may learn Disciplines under the same rules as Kindred </b></i>means.<br /> <br /> Tell me what a &quot;Standard Discipline technique&quot; is. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 01-20-2017, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T17:06:51-08:00","id":1035528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035500#post1035500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am not sure what that wiki is, but I generally don't look at Wiki's online because half the time I can't tell if they are Old Wod or New wod or Chronicles. So I tend to look directly in the book... which everyone seems to be ignoring the fact that the book states:<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Learning Disciplines: Ghouls may learn Disciplines under the same rules as Kindred. </b></i>They may not learn Coils or Scales of the Dragon. Page 297<br /> <br /> <br /> So that means everything in the section where it describes how Kindred learn disciplines is EXACTLY THE SAME for a ghoul. How is this not recognized? I did not say that kindred was an interchangeable word to be tossed around whenever all willynilly. I did not say that ghouls are kindred... I said the book said to follow the same rules as the kindred<br /> <br /> The book specifically says to refer to that section of the book and use it. Basic reading comprehension means that if it says to use those rules for how a ghoul worKs, then when it says vampires can teach to other vampires. It means vampires can teach to ghouls too...<br /> <br /> I don't get how we are all ignoring that line? And if i am not reading it correctly: What does it mean?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Do let me know how Majesty is different for a vampire and a ghoul? What are the different mechanical functions? Where can I find how the rest of the disciplines work for Ghouls. Besides failing against a vampire they are mechanically 100% the same. Charm still charms. Dominate still Dominates. Protean still.... proteans? I think you misunderstood me<br /> <br /> But this is a perfect teachable example because you said they work the same EXCEPT in these certain situations. So when it says ghouls learn the way vampires do EXCEPT when it's Ordo stuff... that would mean all instances where it says a vampire can teach a vampire would mean a vampire can teach a ghoul.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, If am wrong tell me what this <i><b> Ghouls may learn Disciplines under the same rules as Kindred </b></i>means.<br /> <br /> Tell me what a &amp;quot;Standard Discipline technique&amp;quot; is. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Any disciple that require leaking blood infused with Vitae, because Ghouls can leak vitae as a fluid like Vampires can. Aside from that, nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T20:00:30-08:00","id":1035597,"title":"","content":"As much as I hate to break up an argument, even one that appear pointless to me, I feel the need to point out that Kindred consider devotions trade secrets so are very careful about teaching them. Ghouls will not easily find a teacher. That aside I think the standard should be to find where it says ghouls can't learn devotions because when the book says they can learn as Kindred then they should learn as Kindred except where indicated otherwise. Devotions, blood sorcery, and coils are all disciplines and use the same rules except when noted otherwise. If something inhibits disciplines then that would include devotions, for instance, unless indicating otherwise. That does not mean something inhibiting blood sorcery need do anything to coils. I find the argument pointless because when talking about the niche of a niche should it not be to each their own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T00:24:10-08:00","id":1035649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035500#post1035500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So that means everything in the section where it describes how Kindred learn disciplines is EXACTLY THE SAME for a ghoul. How is this not recognized? I did not say that kindred was an interchangeable word to be tossed around whenever all willynilly. I did not say that ghouls are kindred... I said the book said to follow the same rules as the kindred<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, from the top because you're clearly not getting it:<br /> <br /> Kindred and ghouls learn <b>disciplines</b> in the exact same way.<br /> <br /> <b>Kindred</b> learn disciplines and devotions in the exact same way.<br /> <br /> This <b>does not mean </b>that <b>ghouls</b> can learn disciplines and devotions in the exact same way.<br /> <br /> Disciplines <b>are not devotions.</b><br /> <br /> Ghouls <b>are not Kindred.</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T04:02:24-08:00","id":1035674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035597#post1035597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I hate to break up an argument, even one that appear pointless to me, I feel the need to point out that Kindred consider devotions trade secrets so are very careful about teaching them. Ghouls will not easily find a teacher. That aside I think the standard should be to find where it says ghouls can't learn devotions because when the book says they can learn as Kindred then they should learn as Kindred except where indicated otherwise. Devotions, blood sorcery, and coils are all disciplines and use the same rules except when noted otherwise. If something inhibits disciplines then that would include devotions, for instance, unless indicating otherwise. That does not mean something inhibiting blood sorcery need do anything to coils. I find the argument pointless because when talking about the niche of a niche should it not be to each their own?</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree, where something is not straight up answered, that would make sense as the default assumption until corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T07:35:20-08:00","id":1035705,"title":"","content":"I think it's more <i>interesting</i> if they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T10:30:01-08:00","id":1035750,"title":"","content":"Given how many times writers have remembered to say that they can't (reverent and blood god) I'd be inclined to believe that they can unless stated otherwise, it could be wrong but if I need to make the call that's how I would go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T14:58:01-08:00","id":1035849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035649#post1035649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, from the top because you're clearly not getting it:<br /> <br /> Kindred and ghouls learn <b>disciplines</b> in the exact same way.<br /> <br /> <b>Kindred</b> learn disciplines and devotions in the exact same way.<br /> <br /> This <b>does not mean </b>that <b>ghouls</b> can learn disciplines and devotions in the exact same way.<br /> <br /> Disciplines <b>are not devotions.</b><br /> <br /> Ghouls <b>are not Kindred.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kindred learn Disciplines a certain way.<br /> <br /> Devotions are learned just as Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Ghouls can learn Disciplines as Kindred, unless noted otherwise.<br /> <br /> It is natural to follow Ghouls can learn Devotions as they are learned by Kindred the same as Disciplines, just like Ghouls also learn, and nothing states that they can't.<br /> <br /> But Diggs already stated something similar, to no avail. So this is my howl at the wind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T03:43:28-08:00","id":1036011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035849#post1035849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Devotions are learned just as Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once a vampire knows<br /> a Devotion, she can teach it <b><i>to another Kindred</i></b> in much the<br /> same way as the standard Discipline techniques. </div> </div> </div><b>ANOTHER KINDRED</b><br /> <br /> Not a ghoul, another vampire.<br /> <br /> Ghouls can learn <b>disciplines<i>. </i></b>For the last time, <b><i>devotions are not disciplines.</i></b> So<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035849#post1035849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghouls can learn Disciplines as Kindred, unless noted otherwise.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is entirely irrelevant. You can learn a devotion <i>in the same <b>way</b> as a discipline</i> if you are a <b><i>Vampire. </i></b><br /> <br /> They are <i><b>not the same</b></i> <i><b>thing.</b></i><br /> <br /> So in conclusion<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035849#post1035849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is natural to follow Ghouls can learn Devotions as they are learned by Kindred the same as Disciplines</div> </div> </div> </div>No it isn't<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1035849#post1035849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nothing states that they can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T05:02:01-08:00","id":1036025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036011#post1036011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/I][/B]For the last time, <b><i>devotions are not disciplines.</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Except of course, that in all this you've yet to cite a passage that conclusively states this.<br /> <br /> You've asserted it for three whole pages without a single citation of anything that proves it to be the case, and without any acknowledgement of the various bits of text that have been cited.<br /> <br /> As well, you've tried to use logic that doesn't work. Your argument comes down to trying to claim that a rule that applies to rectangles doesn't apply to squares, because squares and rectangles aren't the same thing. Which is, of course, absurd because all squares are rectangles. It doesn't matter if a rule applies to some rectangles that doesn't apply to squares. That doesn't stop all squares from being rectangles. If a rule says it applies to rectangles it should be assumed to apply to squares unless there is an explicit statement to the contrary.<br /> <br /> The more you shout, &quot;Devotions aren't Disciplines&quot; as the sum total of your argument, the more you're saying nobody should care about what you're saying since you're making it abundantly clear that you don't care about the best way to interpret the text instead of the most efficient way to get everyone that disagrees with you to shut up and leave the thread so you can feel like you &quot;won.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, I hope my reputation for being stubborn about forum debates precedes me, because I'm willing to go back and forth on this until you give up if that's the game you want to play. Because your reading of the text is absurd, and I think there is zero compelling reasons outside of a critical reading of the text to consider your less accurate assessment of the text as being more useful to running the game.<br /> <br /> Also, the 1e Ghoul book explicitly stated that Ghouls can learn Devotions... so there's that to contend with as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T05:34:51-08:00","id":1036028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036025#post1036025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your argument comes down to trying to claim that a rule that applies to rectangles doesn't apply to squares, because squares and rectangles aren't the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it doesn't.<br /> <br /> For one thing, there is already a type of being that can learn one and not the other: Revenants. If disciplines and devotions were the same thing then the notion that they could learn one but not the other is what would be absurd.<br /> <br /> Revenants are also my primary objection to giving ghouls devotions for another reason. Ghouls can <i>become</i> revenants, and revenants can subsequently become vampires. It wouldn't make any sense for a ghoul to learn a devotion, lose the ability to use it if they died and rose as a revenant, and then re-learn it if they were uplifted.<br /> <br /> It's not like being able to retain vitae in their system. That's a physiological process. This is something they've <i>learned.</i><br /> <br /> Also that last post was pretty much the final fucks I give about this topic leaving my body, so I'm out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 01-22-2017, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T08:17:06-08:00","id":1036079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036025#post1036025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except of course, that in all this you've yet to cite a passage that conclusively states this.<br /> <br /> You've asserted it for three whole pages without a single citation of anything that proves it to be the case, and without any acknowledgement of the various bits of text that have been cited.<br /> <br /> As well, you've tried to use logic that doesn't work. Your argument comes down to trying to claim that a rule that applies to rectangles doesn't apply to squares, because squares and rectangles aren't the same thing. Which is, of course, absurd because all squares are rectangles. It doesn't matter if a rule applies to some rectangles that doesn't apply to squares. That doesn't stop all squares from being rectangles. If a rule says it applies to rectangles it should be assumed to apply to squares unless there is an explicit statement to the contrary.<br /> <br /> The more you shout, &amp;quot;Devotions aren't Disciplines&amp;quot; as the sum total of your argument, the more you're saying nobody should care about what you're saying since you're making it abundantly clear that you don't care about the best way to interpret the text instead of the most efficient way to get everyone that disagrees with you to shut up and leave the thread so you can feel like you &amp;quot;won.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Well, I hope my reputation for being stubborn about forum debates precedes me, because I'm willing to go back and forth on this until you give up if that's the game you want to play. Because your reading of the text is absurd, and I think there is zero compelling reasons outside of a critical reading of the text to consider your less accurate assessment of the text as being more useful to running the game.<br /> <br /> Also, the 1e Ghoul book explicitly stated that Ghouls can learn Devotions... so there's that to contend with as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because you can't provide a citation proving the book does not say something. The point is, the book doesn't say ghouls can learn devotions. The book does say ghouls can learn most disciplines. A valid interpretation of that statement is &quot;ghouls are not capable of learning all disciplines.&quot; Especially since it proceeds to list restrictions on discipline use and diminished returns on the results.<br /> I reject the premise that Devotion is just another interchangeable term for Discipline. But even if I were to accept it for the sake of argument, that doesn't mean ghouls are qualified to learn them. If standard discipline ranks are prohibited or function at diminished functionality for ghouls, what on earth makes you think they are capable or even qualified to use a highly specialized version of a power when they are already employing a watered down version of the devotion's prequisites in the first place?<br /> The answer to that depends on the game's individual setting.<br /> <br /> As for the first edition Ghouls book. You seem to have forgotten that it also says a discipline that would generate a direct mental or emotional effect against their target would fail outright if that ghoul's target is a vampire. And disciplines and devotions cost twice the experience to learn. <br /> <br /> So let's apply some critical thinking.<br /> <br /> Devotions have a separate entry in the book, separate from disciplines, separate from coils, separate from merits, separate from cruac, separate from scales (which are kind of like the coils version of devotions), and separate from Theban Sorcery. The book says, in the section about devotions, that Kindred can develop devotions and teach other kindred. There is no mention of ghouls being able to use them.<br /> In the section about ghouls, it does not say they can use devotions. Nor does it say they can use blood sorcery or scales, or coils. It says they can use <b>most</b> Disciplines. Not all. And if you go to those respective entries and read the mechanics, it should be obvious why they can't use them. <br /> <br /> But since we are now applying the logic of &quot;if the book doesn't forbid it, therefore it's okay&quot; then that means werewolves and mages can learn disciplines. After all the book does mention their existence and since the book doesn't say they can't learn disciplines and devotions, that means they can learn them. For that matter, kindred can go out and get a Mack Truck and teach it Juggernaut's Gait. After all, there's nothing in the book saying they can't. And there's plenty of examples of vampire powers being littered all over the place or passed on to other characters and objects to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:50:15-08:00","id":1036132,"title":"","content":"Oh-key...<br /> <br /> I should have expected that a simple question would lead to a 3-page knife fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:59:42-08:00","id":1036166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036028#post1036028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No it doesn't.<br /> <br /> For one thing, there is already a type of being that can learn one and not the other: Revenants. If disciplines and devotions were the same thing then the notion that they could learn one but not the other is what would be absurd.<br /> <br /> Revenants are also my primary objection to giving ghouls devotions for another reason. Ghouls can <i>become</i> revenants, and revenants can subsequently become vampires. It wouldn't make any sense for a ghoul to learn a devotion, lose the ability to use it if they died and rose as a revenant, and then re-learn it if they were uplifted.<br /> <br /> It's not like being able to retain vitae in their system. That's a physiological process. This is something they've <i>learned.</i><br /> <br /> Also that last post was pretty much the final fucks I give about this topic leaving my body, so I'm out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given that the book explicitly states that Revenants can't, wouldn't it then follow that the writers would also have included that caveat for Ghouls if they can not? Precedence shows that the writers include text preventing the learning of Devotions if the fact is relevant. Assuming that they didn't, in the absence of evidence, simply doesn't follow.<br /> <br /> More importantly, <i>Vampires</i> can become Revenants. By this logic, Vampires can't learn Devotions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire FAQ</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revenants have Blood Potency 1 (see p. 94). However, if a supernatural effect would strip one of the Kindred to Blood Potency 0 or lower, the vampire instead becomes a Blood Potency 1 revenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty simple.<br /> <br /> A=B for the purposes of learning C<br /> D=C for the purposes of teaching (to B, but we've already established that A=B for the purposes of learning)<br /> <br /> B can learn C (and therefore D by substitution)<br /> A can learn D<br /> <br /> Where A is Ghouls, B is Vampires, C is Disciplines, and D is Devotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:15:27-08:00","id":1036178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036166#post1036166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Given that the book explicitly states that Revenants can't, wouldn't it then follow that the writers would also have included that caveat for Ghouls if they can not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Revenants are stated to be <i>identical</i> to kindred except where their sidebar says otherwise. So if their discipline restrictions had not mentioned excluding devotions, it would have been reasonable to assume they could learn them.<br /> <br /> Ghouls, on the other hand <i>aren't vampires</i>. So the same assumption is not guaranteed to be valid there. <br /> <br /> I will concede that I forgot about vampires reverting to revenant-hood if they lose their last blood potency point, but ultimately I don't think that itself is an issue. You see, we know that when elders lose blood potency, they retain attributes and skills developed above their new cap. The same principle could apply to vampires in this case. <br /> <br /> I still don't like it. Revenants are more vampire than ghouls, so they should not have less capacity to master the powers of the blood. It doesn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:22:36-08:00","id":1036183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036079#post1036079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's because you can't provide a citation proving the book does not say something. The point is, the book doesn't say ghouls can learn devotions. The book does say ghouls can learn most disciplines. A valid interpretation of that statement is &quot;ghouls are not capable of learning all disciplines.&quot; Especially since it proceeds to list restrictions on discipline use and diminished returns on the results.<br /> I reject the premise that Devotion is just another interchangeable term for Discipline. But even if I were to accept it for the sake of argument, that doesn't mean ghouls are qualified to learn them. If standard discipline ranks are prohibited or function at diminished functionality for ghouls, what on earth makes you think they are capable or even qualified to use a highly specialized version of a power when they are already employing a watered down version of the devotion's prequisites in the first place?<br /> The answer to that depends on the game's individual setting.<br /> <br /> As for the first edition Ghouls book. You seem to have forgotten that it also says a discipline that would generate a direct mental or emotional effect against their target would fail outright if that ghoul's target is a vampire. And disciplines and devotions cost twice the experience to learn.<br /> <br /> So let's apply some critical thinking.<br /> <br /> Devotions have a separate entry in the book, separate from disciplines, separate from coils, separate from merits, separate from cruac, separate from scales (which are kind of like the coils version of devotions), and separate from Theban Sorcery. The book says, in the section about devotions, that Kindred can develop devotions and teach other kindred. There is no mention of ghouls being able to use them.<br /> In the section about ghouls, it does not say they can use devotions. Nor does it say they can use blood sorcery or scales, or coils. It says they can use <b>most</b> Disciplines. Not all. And if you go to those respective entries and read the mechanics, it should be obvious why they can't use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright alright. Critical thinking.<br /> <br /> Devotions have a subsection in the Discipline chapter and the only thing that's not really a 'discipline' in that chapter is the Ordo stuff, which it points out ( and is ironically the only thing that ghouls are banned from learning ) Not an entirely seperate entry, or chapter. They aren't listed in a new part, they are listed in the Discipline part. A part of the book that calls them &gt;Discipline techniques&lt; No they are not entirely new disciplines, that is true, but they are PART of the disciplines that exist.<br /> <br /> What is a standard discipline technique? They are mentioned under the Discipline Technique section (Also known as Devotions )<br /> <br /> <br /> Example: You have to know Majesty to know Awe. But once you know Majesty you can know/learn the rest of it. Awe, Confidant Green Eyes, Enthrall Idol....and Summoning. Wouldn't it be safe to assume that each of these steps on the Majesty track are the standard discipline Techniques and with careful practice and honing of your discipline you can learn nonstandard ones?<br /> <br /> Or even Dominate, there are 5 dots but I believe conditioning could be a 6th.<br /> <br /> If I am entirely wrong on this please please. I ask again WHAT THE HELL IS A STANDARD DISCIPLINE TECHNIQUE?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036079#post1036079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But since we are now applying the logic of &quot;if the book doesn't forbid it, therefore it's okay&quot; then that means werewolves and mages can learn disciplines. After all the book does mention their existence and since the book doesn't say they can't learn disciplines and devotions, that means they can learn them. For that matter, kindred can go out and get a Mack Truck and teach it Juggernaut's Gait. After all, there's nothing in the book saying they can't. And there's plenty of examples of vampire powers being littered all over the place or passed on to other characters and objects to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages and Werewolves also do not have a section in their book where it says that they may learn disciplines as vampires do. No one is saying &quot;Just because it doesn't say we can't, then we can&quot; There have been page numbers, book citations and direct evidence to the book where basic reading comprehension would imply that it is acceptable<br /> <br /> <br /> The few people who are asking for why it doesn't work also seem to be asking for book evidence and quotes and explainations. on why not just &quot;Well it doesn't verbatim say so&quot; So therefore we can't<br /> <br /> The book doesn't expressly say vampires don't shit rainbows and fly around leaving sparkles behind either... but we all know from the text. that these vampires are not like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 01-22-2017, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:30:51-08:00","id":1036190,"title":"","content":"Standard discipline techniques are the ones revenants can learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:32:41-08:00","id":1036193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036190#post1036190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Standard discipline techniques are the ones revenants can learn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where in the book does it explain that? Please provide an example. After looking over the Revenant section I see nothing of the sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:50:28-08:00","id":1036203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036178#post1036178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revenants are more vampire than ghouls, so they should not have less capacity to master the powers of the blood. It doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take issue with this assertion. As I've said before. Revenants are mistakes. Aborted abominations. They are accidental, and they can be created without ever having tasted Vitae. They are worse than Ghouls in just about every way, even ignoring the Devotion thing. Ghouls are a deliberate act of creation, and they require Vitae rather than just having been bit at some point in the past. Vampires actively avoid the creation of Revenants.<br /> <br /> Ghouls are closer to Vampires than Revenants are.<br /> <br /> Ghouls can even learn Blood Sorcery, whereas Revenants may not; this alone is precedence enough that Ghouls can learn more than Revenants can, even if Ghouls can't use Cruac rituals after the first dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:40:58-08:00","id":1036249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036193#post1036193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Where in the book does it explain that? Please provide an example. After looking over the Revenant section I see nothing of the sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if they can't use devotions, what else would you call the things they <i>can</i> use?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036203#post1036203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls are closer to Vampires than Revenants are.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. No they are not.<br /> <br /> Ghouls are humans empowered by vampiric blood.<br /> <br /> Revenants are blood-sucking monsters who burn in sunlight.<br /> <br /> Y'know, <i>vampires. </i><br /> <br /> I don't give a shit if they're &quot;mistakes&quot; or &quot;have never tasted vitae&quot; <i>they can make their own. </i>If that doesn't qualify you what the fuck does?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:52:22-08:00","id":1036257,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry that the fact that Revenants are weaker and worse off than Ghouls in every single way except the ability to feed is somehow personally offensive to you (as evidenced by your need to cuss me out), but it's also not really a part of this discussion.<br /> <br /> You glossed over the important part: Ghouls can learn Disciplines that Revenants can not. Using the inability of Revenants to learn something is, therefore, not evidence that Ghouls also cannot learn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:03:49-08:00","id":1036269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036257#post1036257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls can learn Disciplines that Revenants can not.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they can't. Revenants can learn unique disciplines in the same manner as out of clan vampires can, By ingesting a point of vitae from the person teaching them. Ghouls naturally do this with any regnant, which is what allows them to learn disciplines at all. <br /> <br /> But seriously, can you please unpack how on earth you came to the conclusion that humans with blood-based magic powers are closer to vampires that <i>actual blood-drinking walking corpses.</i><br /> <br /> I'm genuinely struggling to wrap my head around this. You say &quot;except the ability to feed&quot; as if it's not <i>the defining quality of vampire-hood. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:07:58-08:00","id":1036271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036028#post1036028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please actually provide solid argumentation for this assertion; which is the whole problem with your approach to this thread anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For one thing, there is already a type of being that can learn one and not the other: Revenants. If disciplines and devotions were the same thing then the notion that they could learn one but not the other is what would be absurd. </div> </div> </div>As has been noted, this does not hold up. First thing, Ghouls can learn things Revenants can't. Second, the line from the book that lists what Revenants can't learn are all &quot;advanced&quot; applications of Disicplines (aka they're not that basic core Disicplines techniques, they're Devotions, blood sorcery, and Coils/Scales). Revenants are unquestionably restricted to standard Discipline techniques, and Ghouls are unquestionably not restricted to just standard Discipline techniques (there is no question they can learn blood sorcery and Bloodline Disicplines).<br /> <br /> So this doesn't bolster your point, and in fact reduces the value of it for how one approaches the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Revenants are also my primary objection to giving ghouls devotions for another reason. Ghouls can <i>become</i> revenants, and revenants can subsequently become vampires. It wouldn't make any sense for a ghoul to learn a devotion, lose the ability to use it if they died and rose as a revenant, and then re-learn it if they were uplifted. </div> </div> </div>This is also true of a Ghoul that learns Theban Sorcery. Either leave the dots on their sheet and have them been inaccessible, until uplifted, or they lose it. Honestly, a ghoul that becomes a Revenant and then gets uplifted to a full vampire that has paid the price of losing a power or two... has still ended up with the far better bargain. If you were a recently uplifted vampire, who then finds out that they forgot tricks of the blood they knew as a ghoul, would you want to go back to being a Revenant just to spite having to relearn those tricks?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is something they've <i>learned.</i> </div> </div> </div>You can forget things you've learned, even if the games generally do not model this. There's also a whole slew of Merits that a Ghoul can lose if they get Embraced; those are just explicitly covered by the Sanctity of Merits rules as to what to do about that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036079#post1036079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's because you can't provide a citation proving the book does not say something.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is your counter-argument to my point, then you're acknowledging that Elfive is incorrect.<br /> <br /> Elfive is making an assertive statement, that the books do say something (in this case that the books say Devotions aren't Disciplines). Asking for citation to back this up is completely warranted.<br /> <br /> If you're acknowledging that the books don't say that Devotions aren't Disciplines, then you're acknowledging that this should not be cited as factual gospel with the vehemence that has apparently worn Elfive out already.<br /> <br /> However, that gets to the more important question of - given all the evidence at hand - should Devotions be treated as Disicplines in the specific context of Ghouls learning powers while there is no 2e statement on the subject. Even then though, this requires positive assertive statements that can be backed by citations of the books. If you want to say that the best reading of the books is that Devotions should not be treated this way, you have to demonstrate it. You're trying to prove a positive assertion (aka that the books support reading the text in a specific fashion), not assert a negative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point is, the book doesn't say ghouls can learn devotions. The book does say ghouls can learn most disciplines. A valid interpretation of that statement is &quot;ghouls are not capable of learning all disciplines.&quot; Especially since it proceeds to list restrictions on discipline use and diminished returns on the results. </div> </div> </div>Valid? Sure, but there's more evidence at hand than this to weigh if it is the best reading. The fact that it specifies what a Ghoul can't learn and doesn't include Devotions. The fact that Revenants are specifically stated to be unable to learn Devotions, but ghouls are not. The fact that 1e Ghouls have the same essential learning restrictions as 2e Ghouls, but 1e clarified that ghouls can learn Devotions. The way that the book describes Discipline and Devotions is much more strongly weighted towards treating Devotions as Disciplines for the purposes of what a character can or cannot learn. Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I reject the premise that Devotion is just another interchangeable term for Discipline. </div> </div> </div>This is a strawman. Nobody is asserting that Devotion and Discipline are interchangeable. This is my rectangles and squares point. All Devotions are Disciplines for this purpose, but not all Disciplines are Devotions. The same holds true for how the books treat blood sorcery and Coils/Scales.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If standard discipline ranks are prohibited or function at diminished functionality for ghouls, what on earth makes you think they are capable or even qualified to use a highly specialized version of a power when they are already employing a watered down version of the devotion's prequisites in the first place? </div> </div> </div>No standard Discipline ranks are prohibited from being learned, or are functionally diminished in 2e. There are powers they can learn but not use at all, and Ghoul Discipline use is blanket weaker against vampires in specific ways (regardless of being &quot;standard&quot; or not). And the book explicitly states that Ghouls can purchase powers they can't use as prerequisites for ones they can. So the book completely supports the idea of Ghouls learning a standard Discipline technique they can't even use, as a stepping stone to higher ranked standard Discipline technique. The jump from standard to non-standard is not exactly significant here. It makes as much sense for a Ghoul to be able to learn Disicpline X's third dot that they can't use just to buy the fourth dot, as it does for them to learn a Devotion that uses said third dot as a prerequisite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The answer to that depends on the game's individual setting. </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the first edition Ghouls book. You seem to have forgotten that it also says a discipline that would generate a direct mental or emotional effect against their target would fail outright if that ghoul's target is a vampire. And disciplines and devotions cost twice the experience to learn. </div> </div> </div>Yes, there are explicit changes made between the editions. Learning Devotions has yet to be explicitly changed. Ghoul's using Disciplines on vampires has been changed to emphasize blood sympathy over mental/emotional effects, and the XP system in 2e has been radically changed across the board. Nothing about what things a Ghouls can learn things has changed, even if the books did not include a supplemental 1e clarification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Devotions have a separate entry in the book, separate from disciplines, separate from coils, separate from merits, separate from cruac, separate from scales (which are kind of like the coils version of devotions), and separate from Theban Sorcery. The book says, in the section about devotions, that Kindred can develop devotions and teach other kindred. There is no mention of ghouls being able to use them. </div> </div> </div>This is a failure of critical thinking. Blood sorcery and Coils/Scales are explicitly Disciplines. If they have separate sections it is more supportive of the idea that Devotions are part of the broader umbrella of &quot;Discipline.&quot; Devotions are also between the standard Disciplines and the special Disciplines; whereas Merits are a separate section completely. If the book writers didn't want us to associate Devotions with Disciplines directly... why are they placed in the middle of the Disciplines section?<br /> <br /> As well, critical thinking, instead of semantic nitpicking, would say that the most obvious intent of the text is that Ghouls learning Discipline-stuff follows the same rules as vampires learning Discipline-stuff unless explicitly noted (which it is only for Coils/Scales). If the text specifically says, &quot;can learn this stuff like a kindred except for X,Y,Z,&quot; and Devotions are not X, Y, or Z, <u>and a similar section for a different group does include Devotions when discussing restrictions on learning special Disciplines</u>, the evidence of critical thought is vastly on the side of, &quot;the intent of the rules is for Ghouls to be capable of learning Devotions.&quot; The Devotion section doesn't need to talk about whether or not Ghouls can learn them. The Devotion section just needs to show that Devotions are a special form of Disciplines, like blood sorcery or Coils/Scales, and the Ghouls section then specifies what they can learn (which is any standard or special Discipline besides Coils/Scales).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the section about ghouls, it does not say they can use devotions. Nor does it say they can use blood sorcery or scales, or coils. </div> </div> </div>You know the critical reading means not stopping at the first line right?<br /> <br /> &quot;Learning Disciplines: Ghouls may learn Disciplines under the same rules as Kindred. They may not learn Coils or Scales of the Dragon.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's how the Ghoul section expands on what it means when it says, &quot;most.&quot; Right there. It says not Coils/Scales explicitly, and does not explicitly state any other special Discipline is off limits. If they wanted to include blood sorcery or Devotions, they would have, just like they did with Revenants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But since we are now applying the logic of &quot;if the book doesn't forbid it, therefore it's okay&quot; then that means werewolves and mages can learn disciplines. </div> </div> </div>What happened to this attempt to apply critical thinking to all this? Because that's just plain old bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 01-22-2017, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:20:21-08:00","id":1036275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036269#post1036269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No they can't. Revenants can learn unique disciplines in the same manner as out of clan vampires can, By ingesting a point of vitae from the person teaching them. Ghouls naturally do this with any regnant, which is what allows them to learn disciplines at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to reiterate a specific point in my bigger post:<br /> <br /> Bloodline Disciplines clearly disprove this assertion. Ghouls can learn Bloodline Disciplines, Revenants cannot, despite neither normally capable of being a part of a Bloodline.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:25:58-08:00","id":1036276,"title":"","content":"Oh, right, those things. <br /> <br /> Eh, whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:14:37-08:00","id":1036326,"title":"","content":"Disclaimer: I don't really have a horse in this race. I think both &quot;ghouls can learn Devotions&quot; and &quot;ghouls cannot learn Devotions&quot; are valid interpretations of the text, and unless/until Half Damned comes along and clarifies this point, I'm going with &quot;whatever the ST feels is most appropriate for their game.&quot; For me, that's usually going to mean &quot;yes, but they require a teacher&quot; because that gives me more plot hook fodder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036271#post1036271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this is your counter-argument to my point, then you're acknowledging that Elfive is incorrect.<br /> <br /> Elfive is making an assertive statement, that the books do say something (in this case that the books say Devotions aren't Disciplines). Asking for citation to back this up is completely warranted.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Elfive is not making an assertive statement that the book says Devotions aren't Disciplines (not that it would be a difficult assertion to find supporting evidence for - they have different names.) Rather, Elfive is challenging the assertive statement that the book says Devotions are Disciplines. So far, the supporting evidence that has been raised in response to that challenge mainly consists of them appearing in the same section of the book (although under a different header), the Devotions section describing them as &quot;Discipline techniques&quot; (though not as &quot;Disciplines&quot; <i>per se</i>). YMMV on if that's enough evidence to confirm the assertion that Devotions are Disciplines, though it isn't enough to convince me. It has also been brought up that the Rules for Revenants sidebar calls out Devotions as a thing Revenants cannot learn while the Ghouls section does not, which is pretty convincing evidence in support of the assertion that Ghouls can learn Devotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:34:26-08:00","id":1036355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036326#post1036326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Elfive is not making an assertive statement that the book says Devotions aren't Disciplines (not that it would be a difficult assertion to find supporting evidence for - they have different names.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Elfive has repeatedly asserted that Devotions aren't Disciplines. If you wish to read their posts more charitably, that's kind of you, but this does not strike me as a honest reading of the thread so far. Elfive has repeatedly in bold letters, stated this position as a matter of fact with no evidence from the book, or no logical extrapolation from the book.<br /> <br /> As well, what you're responding to was an assertion that my argument was invalid because of the &quot;cannot prove a negative&quot; issue, which has nothing to do with the merit of what was said.<br /> <br /> And yes, they have different names. But the book has lots of names of special Disciplines (Devotions, blood sorcery, Coils/Scales). If Devotions aren't Disciplines because they have a different name to connote their special function... why is Cruac a Discipline?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rather, Elfive is challenging the assertive statement that the book says Devotions are Disciplines. </div> </div> </div>I think tsusasi deserves far more credit for attempting to engage with this.<br /> <br /> As well, nobody has asserted that the book outright says Devotions are Disciplines, but that the evidence at hand all points to them as part of the larger umbrella of Disciplines, and thus should be considered Disciplines as for the purpose of the question at hand. Attempting to challenge an assertion nobody is actually making is what we call a strawman. Everyone arguing for Ghouls being able to learn them acknowledges it is a matter of extrapolation (or is arguing from a different perspective such as preferring the story options it upholds) from the text since there's a lack of a definitive statement in the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So far, the supporting evidence that has been raised in response to that challenge mainly consists of them appearing in the same section of the book (although under a different header), the Devotions section describing them as &quot;Discipline techniques&quot; (though not as &quot;Disciplines&quot; <i>per se</i>). </div> </div> </div>As I went into, &quot;appearing in the same section,&quot; includes being sandwiched between sections with different headers that are all things that there is no valid reading as not-Disicplines. Unless you want to argue that blood sorcery or Coils/Scales aren't Disciplines, the &quot;under a different header but in the same section,&quot; is not a significant counter-point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T18:00:10-08:00","id":1036374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036355#post1036355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elfive has repeatedly asserted that Devotions aren't Disciplines. If you wish to read their posts more charitably, that's kind of you, but this does not strike me as a honest reading of the thread so far. Elfive has repeatedly in bold letters, stated this position as a matter of fact with no evidence from the book, or no logical extrapolation from the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Him stating it bluntly doesn't change the fact that the burden of proof isn't on him. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036355#post1036355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, what you're responding to was an assertion that my argument was invalid because of the &quot;cannot prove a negative&quot; issue, which has nothing to do with the merit of what was said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, and I was agreeing with Tausai that arguing Elfive is wrong because he can't prove Devotions <i>aren't</i> Disciplines isn't logically sound.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036355#post1036355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, they have different names. But the book has lots of names of special Disciplines (Devotions, blood sorcery, Coils/Scales). If Devotions aren't Disciplines because they have a different name to connote their special function... why is Cruac a Discipline?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cruac is explicitly and unambiguously called a Discipline in the book. &quot;Cruac is a Discipline&quot; is an assertion that can be difinitively proven with citations from the text. Devotions, conversely, are not explicitly called Disciplines, though it can and has been argued that they are. And like I said, YMMV on if the evidence in support of that assertion is convincing to you, because it's not unambiguous like it is with Cruac.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036355#post1036355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think tsusasi deserves far more credit for attempting to engage with this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I'll give them due credit for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036355#post1036355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, nobody has asserted that the book outright says Devotions are Disciplines, but that the evidence at hand all points to them as part of the larger umbrella of Disciplines, and thus should be considered Disciplines as for the purpose of the question at hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just saying, I don't think it's unfair to challenge that conclusion on the basis of the evidence not <i>conclusively</i> pointing to that interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036355#post1036355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attempting to challenge an assertion nobody is actually making is what we call a strawman.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036355#post1036355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone arguing for Ghouls being able to learn them acknowledges it is a matter of extrapolation (or is arguing from a different perspective such as preferring the story options it upholds) from the text since there's a lack of a definitive statement in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, as do I. I also acknowledge that it is valid to disagree with that conclusion on the basis of the evidence in support of the idea that Devotions should be treated as Disciplines is not convincing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036355#post1036355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I went into, &quot;appearing in the same section,&quot; includes being sandwiched between sections with different headers that are all things that there is no valid reading as not-Disicplines. Unless you want to argue that blood sorcery or Coils/Scales aren't Disciplines, the &quot;under a different header but in the same section,&quot; is not a significant counter-point.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I went into, the text under the header for blood sorcery <i>does</i> explicitly state that the above are Disciplines, unlike the text under the header for Devotions, so I think it is a valid counter-point. The text under the header for Coils and Scales doesn't explicitly state that they are Disciplines, and in fact contrasts them with Disciplines, and yes, I would argue that they are not Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T19:26:41-08:00","id":1036401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036374#post1036374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Him stating it bluntly doesn't change the fact that the burden of proof isn't on him.</div> </div> </div> </div>The burden of proof isn't on him for simply challenging the other position. The burden of proof is on him after he has blanket dismissed the other side's arguments and declared his own position correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Right, and I was agreeing with Tausai that arguing Elfive is wrong because he can't prove Devotions <i>aren't</i> Disciplines isn't logically sound. </div> </div> </div>And as I said to tsusasi, One of Elfive's statement is wrong because of this. The corollary to the inability to prove a negative, is the inability to assert it as fact. If you care about the logical soundness of an argument, you must agree that it is logically unsound to assert the Devotions aren't Disciplines as a simple matter of fact; as Elfive did repeatedly. Further if you hold to that adherence to logically sound argumentation, if Elfive has such a statement as an essential assumption of a logical proof, the proof itself is unsound.<br /> <br /> This doesn't completely negate the possibility that he could be right anyway. But if we're going to get into &quot;logically sound&quot; my critique remains sound, and the &quot;can't prove a negative&quot; counter-argument is not a proper application of the rules of logic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cruac is explicitly and unambiguously called a Discipline in the book. </div> </div> </div>So are Coils, even if in a different section then where you were looking (see the character creation section).<br /> <br /> This doesn't, however, negate the point being made. &quot;Having a different name,&quot; is not a sufficient data point to say something isn't a Discipline. There are multiple Disciplines that have different names. Yes, there remains the lack of definitive statement about Devotions, but this particular argument (Devotions have a different name) is not sound.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm just saying, I don't think it's unfair to challenge that conclusion on the basis of the evidence not <i>conclusively</i> pointing to that interpretation. </div> </div> </div>Sure, however it is unfair to assert that a lack of conclusive evidence justifies a position that you fail to support as well as another position as factually correct. Which is what Elfive did. Elfive arguments are not just, &quot;I'm not sure of this, convince me,&quot; but, &quot;I disagree because Devotions are not Disciplines.&quot; Which is unfair to claim bears no burden of proof, or to affirm without any proof offered/defended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The text under the header for Coils and Scales doesn't explicitly state that they are Disciplines, and in fact contrasts them with Disciplines, and yes, I would argue that they are not Disciplines. </div> </div> </div>Which is why it's important to read the whole text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T19:46:20-08:00","id":1036409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036401#post1036401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are Coils, even if in a different section then where you were looking (see the character creation section).</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a page number, because I'm not seeing where in the character creation section this is explicitly stated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036401#post1036401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't, however, negate the point being made. &quot;Having a different name,&quot; is not a sufficient data point to say something isn't a Discipline. There are multiple Disciplines that have different names. Yes, there remains the lack of definitive statement about Devotions, but this particular argument (Devotions have a different name) is not sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that the Disciplines that have different names (I'm assuming you're referring to Cruac and Theban Sorcery here, not to like... Animalism and Majesty) are explicitly called out as being Disciplines. If being named something other than a Discipline and not being explicitly called out as a Discipline is not sufficient to establish something as not a Discipline, what establishes Banes as not Disciplines?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036401#post1036401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why it's important to read the whole text.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have, and I do not recall any explicit statements that either Devotions or Coils are Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T23:40:29-08:00","id":1036465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036409#post1036409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a page number, because I'm not seeing where in the character creation section this is explicitly stated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 81 considers Coils a Discipline for assigning your starting Discipline dots.<br /> <br /> Page 83 has a list of Disciplines, and Coils are listed there (as are Theban and Cruac); which is the most direct statement. The book gives us a list of Disciplines, it's on the list as opposed to being listed separately or called out as something else.<br /> <br /> Page 84 when discussing purchasing Disciplines, like the p. 81 reference, includes Coils.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except that the Disciplines that have different names (I'm assuming you're referring to Cruac and Theban Sorcery here, not to like... Animalism and Majesty) are explicitly called out as being Disciplines. </div> </div> </div>And Devotions are explicitly called out as &quot;Discipline techniques,&quot; which is referenced to the individual powers within Disciplines as techniques. It's almost like the book is saying that a Devotion is the equivalent of a single power within a full Discipline, rather than being confusing by calling them full Disciplines that only have one power and multiple Discipline prerequisites (which no other Disciplines have).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If being named something other than a Discipline and not being explicitly called out as a Discipline is not sufficient to establish something as not a Discipline, what establishes Banes as not Disciplines? </div> </div> </div>I thought you were trying to take up the mantle of this debate to discuss it under logic and reason, not resort to trollish faux-ad-absurdium arguments that have already gotten this discussion needlessly heated.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T02:28:45-08:00","id":1036504,"title":"","content":"Okay. Here is the deal. If you don't want ghouls learning devotions then you use the book to justify it. You shouldn't try making positions based on picking out statements without considering context. Books weren't written to do that, nor to impede gaming outside of balance issues. Ghouls are balanced in their use of powers not in which powers they can learn, unlike revenants. Some powers just don't work and that gets addressed for ghouls.<br /> <br /> Devotions may be spontaneously manifested. As no terms are giving for how and why that would occur, it is complete ST fiat. Devotions may also be taught by Kindred, except they closely guard them as explicitly stated. Ghouls are not completely trusted by kindred. You don't entrust secrets to addicts. Easy enough to justify that ghouls just don't get an opportunity to learn devotions. If you decide later on that maybe it works out then somebody got a one in a million opportunity. That is how you go about avoiding pointless arguments.<br /> <br /> I consider ghouls learning Theban. It doesn't fit my sensibilities. Can ghouls learn Theban? Sure. I guess so. Maybe. Who cares? Nobody is going to teach a ghoul Theban so it doesn't matter if they can learn it or not. I might even make it against the law, city or LS, either way somebody dies (again).<br /> <br /> It is always better to rule in a way that leaves you more options in the future. How is it not better to say ghouls could learn devotions but they won't because nobody is going to teach them and the circumstances to spontaneously manifest a devotion don't include being a ghoul? That is a rhetorical question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T09:47:35-08:00","id":1036683,"title":"","content":"Honestly, this looks like one of those times when one of the devs should wade in with a simple yes/no answer to this simple yes/no question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T12:25:49-08:00","id":1036764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036011#post1036011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>ANOTHER KINDRED</b><br /> <br /> Not a ghoul, another vampire.<br /> <br /> Ghouls can learn <b>disciplines<i>. </i></b>For the last time, <b><i>devotions are not disciplines.</i></b> So<br /> <br /> <br /> Is entirely irrelevant. You can learn a devotion <i>in the same <b>way</b> as a discipline</i> if you are a <b><i>Vampire. </i></b><br /> <br /> <br /> They are <i><b>not the same</b></i> <i><b>thing.</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>Then why are they (Devotions) discussed under the bullet point &quot;Disciplines&quot; of the &quot;Rules for Revenants&quot; sidebar?<br /> <br /> <br /> Ghouls are as vampires when the matter is learning Disciplines, and people can reasonably assume that Devotions are a subset of Disciplines, like Blood Sorcery and Coils. Being that Ghouls are as Kindred to learn Disciplines they can learn Devotions.<br /> <br /> If you are a Ghoul you are a vampire in matters pertaining the learning of Disciplines, unless stated otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036011#post1036011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in conclusion<br /> <br /> No it isn't<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>In other news;<br /> <br /> Yes it is<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> No it doesn't?<br /> <br /> Is that how one discussess things with you?<br /> <br /> Neither my position nor yours are baseless, unreasonable assumptions. Both are, though, assumptions, not facts.<br /> <br /> A quote from a grand gentleman, Bertrand Russel, that most of us should meditate on and take to heart:<br /> <br /> &quot;The whole problem with the world is that fools and fanatics are always so certain of themselves, but wiser people so full of doubts.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 01-23-2017, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T13:55:11-08:00","id":1036814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036683#post1036683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, this looks like one of those times when one of the devs should wade in with a simple yes/no answer to this simple yes/no question.</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been a few cases where a simple yes or no question ended in all out war .... The Devs I think avoid these threads like the plague <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T16:03:51-08:00","id":1036886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036764#post1036764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> blah</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so basically what I was doing is rejecting the premise that the wording for ghouls and revenants are equivalent. <br /> <br /> Revenants are &quot;vampires unless noted&quot;, so their rules are subtractive. You start with everything a Kindred can do and you then cross off the things listed. <br /> <br /> Ghouls, on the other hand, are &quot;human unless noted&quot;, so their rules are additive. You start by assuming nothing and then <i>add</i> any abilities mentioned. <br /> <br /> This means that the same wording in the two sections can't be assumed to mean the same thing.<br /> <br /> It's a question of context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T16:51:15-08:00","id":1036911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036190#post1036190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Standard discipline techniques are the ones revenants can learn.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036193#post1036193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where in the book does it explain that? Please provide an example. After looking over the Revenant section I see nothing of the sort.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036249#post1036249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if they can't use devotions, what else would you call the things they <i>can</i> use?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think this was glossed over too quick. I'm not sure how much weight it would have in this discussion. However, for those who would like the rules to reflect a consistent metaphysic, it raises good questions regarding the equating of devotions and disciplines.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:42:34-08:00","id":1036975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036814#post1036814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There have been a few cases where a simple yes or no question ended in all out war .... The Devs I think avoid these threads like the plague</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that and the book that's going to have the official answer is in process anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T03:58:11-08:00","id":1037118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1036886#post1036886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so basically what I was doing is rejecting the premise that the wording for ghouls and revenants are equivalent.<br /> <br /> Revenants are &quot;vampires unless noted&quot;, so their rules are subtractive. You start with everything a Kindred can do and you then cross off the things listed.<br /> <br /> Ghouls, on the other hand, are &quot;human unless noted&quot;, so their rules are additive. You start by assuming nothing and then <i>add</i> any abilities mentioned.<br /> <br /> This means that the same wording in the two sections can't be assumed to mean the same thing.<br /> <br /> It's a question of context.</div> </div> </div> </div>This later argument is a good one to support your view on whether Ghouls should or shouldn't be able to learn Devotions, but it is still based on a subjective affirmation that Devotions are not Disciplines when there are reasonable arguments to the contrary. Since it depends on an opinion for it to even matter, it is just an argument to support an opinion, not logical proof of fact.<br /> <br /> Revenants are not Kindred, which is a political term that certain vampires use to refer to themselves.<br /> <br /> Since Devotions can only be learned by Kindred why the need to clarify that Revenants can\u00b4t learn them?<br /> <br /> If Devotions are not Disciplines, why isn't it discussed under it\u00b4s own topic, but instead discussed with everything that is considered a Discipline on page 94 on the &quot;Rules for Revenants&quot; sidebar?<br /> <br /> Why don't you leave the adolescent approach aside and answer the questions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T05:44:22-08:00","id":1037136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1037118#post1037118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Devotions can only be learned by Kindred why the need to clarify that Revenants can\u00b4t learn them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the very first line of the revenant sidebar is<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless noted below, revenants function <b>identically</b> to Kindred. </div> </div> </div>The thing is, devotions <i>are</i> disciplines in one sense, Because disciplines are, in general terms &quot;magic stuff vampires can do&quot;. <br /> <br /> However, they are mechanically distinct. They don't have dot ratings, they don't use discipline experience costs. No devotion has another as a prerequisite. The rules treat them as sepeate things for most purposes. Even the line about them being taught in the same way as disciplines is an in-universe thing. Nobody really teaches anyone anything. You just write the name of the power down on some paper. <br /> <br /> So when the ghoul section says that they can learn <b>disciplines</b> using the same <b>rules</b> as kindred, I read that in the strictest sense possible. The ten groups of five powers actually listed under the section &quot;disciplines&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:15:44-08:00","id":1037152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1037136#post1037136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the very first line of the revenant sidebar is<br /> <br /> <i>Unless noted below, revenants function <b>identically</b> to Kindred</i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This makes complete sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing is, devotions <i>are</i> disciplines in one sense, Because disciplines are, in general terms &quot;magic stuff vampires can do&quot;.<br /> <br /> However, they are mechanically distinct. They don't have dot ratings, they don't use discipline experience costs. No devotion has another as a prerequisite. The rules treat them as sepeate things for most purposes. Even the line about them being taught in the same way as disciplines is an in-universe thing. Nobody really teaches anyone anything. You just write the name of the power down on some paper.<br /> <br /> So when the ghoul section says that they can learn <b>disciplines</b> using the same <b>rules</b> as kindred, I read that in the strictest sense possible. The ten groups of five powers actually listed under the section &quot;disciplines&quot;. </div> </div> </div>And under a sidebar called &quot;<b><i>Rules</i></b> for Revenants&quot;, Devotions are discussed as a subset of Disciplines.<br /> <br /> So this separation of &quot;Disciplines in <i><b>Some Sense</b></i>&quot; and &quot;Not Disciplines for the <b><i>Rules</i></b>&quot; is not consistent with the text, and while it is a reasonable take on the whole thing it is not the <i><b>only</b></i> reasonable take on the whole thing.<br /> <br /> So, reasonably intelligent people can look at it and decide that either of the reasonable interpretations suits their game better, they might even choose to change this for different games they run if they think they can get something thematic out of this distinction.<br /> <br /> One can even argue that this general vaguery on some things is intentional and fits CofD's toolbox design.<br /> <br /> I'm not arguing that your position is wrong, I'm just saying that mine isn't either.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:28:31-08:00","id":1037157,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's probably vague on purpose. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T07:55:42-08:00","id":1037207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1037118#post1037118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't you leave the adolescent approach aside and answer the questions?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#ff0000\">You seem to be having a reasonable discussion here, this wasn't necessary. It's rude at best and a ToU violation at worst, please don't do it again.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T09:20:01-08:00","id":1037251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1033798-can-ghouls-learn-devotions?p=1037207#post1037207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b<span style=\"color:#ff0000\">You seem to be having a reasonable discussion here, this wasn't necessary. It's rude at best and a ToU violation at worst, please don't do it again.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Hello Darksider,<br /> <br /> Can you please clarify how this is a statement worthy of moderation and a possible violation of the terms of use?<br /> <br /> When you quote someone and substitute the words they said for &quot;blah&quot;, that is a childish action, to say nothing of rudeness. I only asked that he drop that kind of attitude so we could discuss the actual matter at hand. And we apparently reached a point of agreement after that. I made no mention of qualities or characteristics of their person, simply called out a behavior that wasn't constructive to the discussion.<br /> <br /> On some threads we have moderators defending people\u00b4s right to be curt, and even to use very polemic and charged words to describe a group of people in the name of free speech, and then in another we have a person being censored for being &quot;rude&quot;.<br /> <br /> The lack of isonomy in the moderators action is understandable, but when the deviations are too significant it is confusing. I am not disputing your assessment, I want to better understand so that I adjust my posting style so this kind of interference is unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Regards,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T10:50:58-08:0